    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city owner capacity rule: creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nChanges made, following the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` pattern already used in this codebase:\n\n1. **`service/CityOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` with a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant, thrown by the service layer so the invariant lives in one place.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added a guard in `saveOwner` for new owners that reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity(owner)` helper:\n   ```java\n   if (owner.isNew()\n       && countOwnersInCity(owner) >= CityOwnerLimitExceededException.MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY) {\n       throw new CityOwnerLimitExceededException(owner.getCity());\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping the new exception to `409 Conflict`, mirroring the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` test (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st create to return 409) passes, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
