    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing conventions of this codebase:\n\n- **Exception in the right unit.** `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` mirrors the sibling `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateHouseholdException` exactly (same package, constructor-builds-message pattern, even the \"Enforcing it in the service layer keeps the invariant in one place\u2026 the REST layer maps this to 409\" docstring convention). Keeping the capacity rule as a service-layer exception is consistent with how the other create-time invariants are enforced.\n- **Handler is idiomatic and additive.** `handleCityOwnerLimitExceededException` is a faithful copy of the adjacent 409 handlers (same `logger.warn` shape, `detailBuild`, `ResponseEntity.status(status)`), placed right after the other duplicate handlers.\n- **Good reuse, no duplication.** The guard reuses the pre-existing `countOwnersInCity(owner)` helper rather than reimplementing the per-city count, and sits alongside the other `owner.isNew()` validation guards at the top of `saveOwner`, matching their ordering and style.\n- **Constant placement is reasonable.** `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` lives on the exception that represents the violated rule and is referenced from the guard, so the limit is defined once.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find this natural; no structural changes needed.",
